# The synthetic E1M2 (T5.3): the corridor's tagged doors (alcoves 3, 7 and
# 12, tag 5, whose ceilings lie above the 124 they open to, so they jump
# there): press the SR raise-door button (line 0, south wall), press it
# again while the doors wait open (busy: nothing), again once they have
# closed onto their floors, then the S1 open-door switch (line 1, west
# wall) once they are idle, and again (spent). Stays in the corridor (the
# lift and floor lines of alcoves 0 and 22 are T5.5's). Written by a
# scratch generator steering the sim.
# T5.4: both lines draw SW1BRCOM, so the dump's textures column checks
# the button turning on and back after 35 tics (twice) and the switch
# turning once.
# forwardmove sidemove turn buttons [xcount]; turn << 8 = angleturn
iwad synthetic
map E1M2
